{
    "background_story": "Loretta was a skilled lawyer who had spent years building a successful career in a prestigious law firm. However, as she approached her 50s, she began to feel unfulfilled and restless. The long hours and high-stakes cases had taken a toll on her personal life, and she yearned for a change. After much contemplation, Loretta made the bold decision to seek quittance from her partnership, opting for an early retirement. She sold her luxurious penthouse apartment and moved to a quaint coastal town, where she bought a small bookstore. Loretta finally found the peace and contentment she had been seeking, surrounded by books and the soothing sound of the ocean. Her decision to leave the fast-paced world of law behind allowed her to rediscover herself and find a new sense of purpose.",
